    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5936c304",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man and a child in a kitchen, with text overlay stating 'I asked him to see things from my point of view' and 'he looked out the kitchen window.' The visual of the child looking out the window while the adult is engaged in cooking or preparing food is juxtaposed with the text to imply that the man is ignoring or not engaging with the speaker's perspective. The meme uses the trope of a woman being relegated to the kitchen, which is a misogynistic stereotype that implies women are confined to domestic roles and are not seen as equal participants in decision-making or perspective-sharing. The overall intent is to humorously or sarcastically criticize a man for not listening or engaging with a woman's viewpoint, while reinforcing the harmful stereotype that women are confined to domestic spaces and are not taken seriously in other contexts. This aligns with the misogynous category as it perpetuates the idea that women's perspectives are less valid or are dismissed by men, and it uses the kitchen as a symbol of domesticity and female roles, which is a common trope in misogynistic humor.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7b6db421"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
